It is Saturday morning and I am helping out in the café.
Elif and I are standing together behind the till.
A customer comes to us at the counter.
"I would like a coffee, please," he says.
"Gladly," I answer.
"Do you also have guest WiFi?" the customer asks.
"Yes, of course," I say and explain it to him.
"Select the network 'Café Gast' on your mobile phone."
"The password is written here on the small card next to the till."
"Just enter the password."
"Mostly that works immediately."
"But sometimes it does not connect the first time."
"Then turn the WiFi off briefly and on again."
The customer takes the card.
"Is the password changed often?" he asks.
"Yes, it is generated anew every month," I answer.
"This month it is simply the word 'Kaffeebohne'."
"All clear, thank you very much," he says and taps on his mobile phone.
Elif hands him the hot cup.
"Here is the coffee," she says, smiling.
